> Module Knockouts_income

> Using Types
> Using Interest as I
> Using Form_w2s as W
> Using Unemployment as U
> Using Form1099_misc as M
> Using Form1099_rs as RS
> Using Social_security as S
> Using Estimated_payments as E
> Using Hsa as H

# Knockouts A: income, HSA and process unsupported situations (issue #36)

Direct File refuses to compute a return, and shows a "knockout" screen, when
the taxpayer is in a situation it does not support. All the situations feed one
fact, `flow.xml` `/flowIsKnockedOut` (`BlockSubmissionOnTrue`; an `Any` over
about 110 facts, lines 11 to 119). This module covers the income, HSA and
process members of that list. `docs/knockout-inventory.md` (generated by
`scripts/gen_knockout_inventory.mjs`) lists every member, its owner and its
status; the household, credit and PTC members belong to issue #37 and the final
aggregation to issue #38.

Policy (`catala/CONVENTIONS.md` section 6): each knockout is an `output`
condition named `ko_` plus the DF fact name, and the calculator reports
"unsupported" instead of a number. The modules merged so far compute their own
knockouts and a per-module `unsupported`. This module

1. instantiates those scopes once (`interest`, `w2`, `unemp`, `misc`, `rs`,
   `ss`, `ep`, `hsa`). Values that the return computes upstream (for example
   `agi`, the HSA contributions reported on W-2s, the Filers answers) are inputs
   here, as in the modules' own tests; the orchestrator wires them in #38;
2. defines the knockouts of `income.xml`, `flow.xml` and `formW2s.xml` that no
   merged module owns (section "Knockouts defined here");
3. exposes a grouped structure per module (`InterestKnockouts`, ...), a flag per
   module, the list of reasons that fired (`fired_knockouts`: one
   `KnockoutReason` constructor per DF fact) and the combined
   `unsupported_income_or_hsa`.

Inputs are complete (CONVENTIONS section 3). Two DF knockout members are dead
code and have no condition here: `/has1099rFormsAndFeatureIsNotEnabled` is the
constant `False` (`form1099Rs.xml` line 41), and the two 1099-R facts for
codes 1 and 3 (`flowKnockoutRetirementQualifiedEarlyDistribution`,
`knockoutDisabilityAndAnotherCode`) can never be true because DF strips the
box 7 code first (`catala/form1099_rs.catala_en`, section on box 7).

